    "pmhnp": "Clinical-style fragments and repetitive r output unrelated to GPU design;256-token diagnostic hit token limit, canonical464-token generation exhausted remaining512 context. No EOS or usable GPU interface.",
    "nativeEnglish": "Raw diagnostic emitted LF ABSTAIN LF then EOS (IDs266,2,70). Canonical training Answer framing emitted Result: -1. LF then EOS (IDs3,288,301,305,302,266,70). Neither is an engineering response; canonical run stopped by model EOS, not output cutoff.",
    "olderLlama": "On-topic outline followed by illustrative C. Initial256 and canonical512 outputs hit caps. Final same-weight greedy attempt reached actual EOS after1749 tokens with previous512-token prefix unchanged. Completion remains non-executable/incomplete as written.",
    "llamaConcreteCodeProblems": [
      "Undeclared OperationType, GPUCommandBuffer and CPUInstructionDecoder types.",
      "Request union defines vertex/color but generated validation uses undefined data.pixel, data.clear and data.copy; result union has pixel but accesses result.x/y.",
      "ValidationResult is passed by value and never returned; caller later prints uninitialized local results.",
      "Zero-value checks assign both expected/actual zero without computing an independent numeric reference. No GPU API dispatch, guest communication or actual comparison is implemented."
    ],
    "attribution": "This text experiment invoked PMHNP-native, native English compositional and older Llama checkpoints. The fixed-symbol Prime10M model received no English GPU design question. No new training, oracle-answer substitution, generated-code execution or tool binding occurred."
  },
